@{
    ViewBag.Title = "Introduction";
}
<div class="col-sm-12">
    <p>
        This site introduces about front-end controls commonly used in many websites of our system.
        For each control, it lists out some use cases which the control or component is frequently applied to.
        In the turn of each use case, it also suggests the most suitable library and how to use that library to overcome the problem.
        The purpose of this is to ensure all users will explore the same user experiences throughout our system.
    </p>
    <p>
        Moreover, the site defines some rules for HTML, CSS/LESS and JavaScript that all front-end developers must follow when taking care of their tasks.
        It aims at improving collaboration, code quality, and enabling supporting infrastructure.
    </p>
    <p>
        For the details, refer to the links below:
        <ul>
            <li>@Html.ActionLink("Html Rules", "HtmlRules", "Home"): defines some rules that you must follow in your HTML code</li>
            <li>@Html.ActionLink("CSS/LESS Rules", "CssRules", "Home"): lists out some common LESS/CSS rules and tips</li>
            <li>@Html.ActionLink("JavaScript Rules", "JavaScriptRules", "Home"): points out some JavaScript's rules and tips to improve the code's quality</li>
        </ul>
    </p>
    <div class="bs-callout bs-callout-warning">
        <h4>Note</h4>
        <p>
            Whatever convention you follow, one of the most important rules is <span class="text-success">"Explain code as needed, where possible"</span>.
            Use comments to explain code:
        </p>
        <ul>
            <li>What does it cover</li>
            <li>What purpose does it serve</li>
            <li>Why is respective solution used or preferred?</li>
        </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="bs-callout bs-callout-info">
        <h4>Supported browsers</h4>
        <p>Our system mainly supports the following browsers:</p>
        <ul>
            <li><a href="http://windows.microsoft.com/en-us/internet-explorer/download-ie" target="_blank">Internet Explorer 8 or older</a></li>
            <li><a href="https://www.mozilla.org/fr/firefox/desktop/" target="_blank">FireFox</a></li>
            <li><a href="http://www.google.com/chrome/" target="_blank">Chrome</a></li>
        </ul>
    </div>
</div>